# ── Step 0: Welcome ────────────────────────────────────────────────
benvida.titulo = Welcome to the Piztu installer
benvida.desc = This wizard will guide you through installing Piztu, the computer classroom management system. You can close and continue later.
benvida.nomes.titulo = 🏷️  Machine names
benvida.nomes.sub = Rename the server and clients before installing
benvida.nomes.corpo = Each machine must have a unique, sequential name:\n  • Server:  tux0\n  • Clients:  tux01, tux02 … tux22  (depending on the number of machines)\n\nOn each machine, edit both files and reboot:\n  sudo nano /etc/hostname\n  sudo nano /etc/hosts\n\nSet the same name in both files and reboot the machine.\n\n(This scheme is just a suggestion: from Piztu you can also add machines with arbitrary names.)
benvida.sudo.titulo = 🔑  Sudo permissions (server and clients)
benvida.sudo.sub = EVERY machine needs passwordless sudo
benvida.sudo.corpo = Same requirement on the server and on the clients. On each machine, run:\n  sudo visudo\n\nAnd add at the end:\n  user ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD:ALL\n\n(replace 'user' with the real user name)\n\n• On the SERVER: the user who opens Piztu. It is needed to install and manage salt-master.\n• On the CLIENTS: the SSH user Ansible/Salt connects with.
benvida.ssh.titulo = 🔐  SSH on the client machines
benvida.ssh.sub = openssh-server is mandatory
benvida.ssh.corpo = Every client machine must have the SSH server installed and active. Install and configure it like this:\n\n  sudo apt update\n  sudo apt install openssh-server\n  nano /etc/ssh/sshd_config\n\nUncomment and edit these lines:\n  Port 22\n  PermitRootLogin yes\n  PubkeyAuthentication yes\n  PasswordAuthentication yes
benvida.aviso = ⚠️  To install in /opt/piztu and create shortcuts, run the installer with sudo.

